tion and maximal velocity.", "children": [{"id": "6b4231a2-2133-4f06-8ceb-1f7eab3bf57f", "type": "concept", "title": "Starts, projection, shin angles, posture, and arm action"}, {"id": "5de559c7-3786-4863-9c43-b52abdafd9c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Stride length, stride frequency, stiffness, and front-side mechanics"}, {"id": "9c227516-9e50-4b3a-8b49-80d92d35c48e", "type": "concept", "title": "Drills, resisted sprints, assisted sprints, and hill work"}]}, {"id": "fc745082-1efd-40f5-9984-eda90e4d77e2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Change of direction", "description": "The gist is to train braking and reorientation, not just running around cones.", "children": [{"id": "ce929deb-6f4c-4a7f-8ead-bd27bf707511", "type": "concept", "title": "Deceleration, plant angles, foot placement, and trunk control"}, {"id": "decec353-e898-42b8-81e4-19cb1474d3ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutting, shuffling, crossover, backpedaling, and reacceleration"}, {"id": "202af281-932e-41a6-80df-d5e586838bf4", "type": "concept", "title": "Planned versus unplanned change-of-direction tasks"}]}, {"id": "2b127dbf-4469-4cf8-8cc6-4002eea2344c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Agility and perception-action skill", "description": "Learners connect physical qualities with decision-making in sport.", "children": [{"id": "8f363d5b-b9d1-4fd1-80d7-c30398ca9881", "type": "concept", "title": "Reaction, scanning, anticipation, and cue recognition"}, {"id": "da123eee-7a4a-4c86-80e3-8c327bc6c625", "type": "concept", "title": "Small-sided games and representative tasks"}, {"id": "8e626241-16cd-4704-820a-1f87d94766c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Testing versus training agility"}]}]}, {"id": "ea2f4a2f-793d-4fbe-beb3-a4733f2b5541", "type": "topic", "title": "Conditioning for Endurance, Repeated Sprint Ability, and Energy Systems", "description": "Program aerobic, anaerobic, interval, and sport-conditioning work with clear physiological targets.", "children": [{"id": "1018770c-3661-464a-8a09-d2ae696fb078", "