 recovery strategies to improve readiness without wasting training time.", "children": [{"id": "0aab04dd-f7ed-4b5c-ac17-686fb785c689", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Flexibility and mobility", "description": "Students learn how range of motion, control, and tolerance differ.", "children": [{"id": "e7cbe2c2-c10a-4099-9390-88d1731d9af8", "type": "concept", "title": "Static, dynamic, ballistic, and proprioceptive neuromuscular facilitation stretching"}, {"id": "4148626f-4fce-4cbc-baa4-3451b8ae46f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Joint mobility, stability, and motor control"}, {"id": "83f7f5ff-d3fb-477f-be78-06ad0219dbc1", "type": "concept", "title": "When more range is helpful, neutral, or risky"}]}, {"id": "bce0ac78-c0b5-4f3d-9c84-cf28999b5d97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Warm-up and preparation", "description": "The point is to prepare the body and mind for the training task ahead.", "children": [{"id": "9d7b7497-5929-4c79-9105-d2b295823cec", "type": "concept", "title": "General and specific warm-ups"}, {"id": "f3b29619-b0fb-4f08-9d65-65b5671d6ec6", "type": "concept", "title": "RAMP-style preparation"}, {"id": "4f5e5014-42d9-4ac2-9bcf-dd2c9be64803", "type": "concept", "title": "Activation, potentiation, rehearsal, and readiness"}]}, {"id": "7f4e1291-10b5-4975-b30c-927067ce319c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Recovery strategies", "description": "Learners evaluate recovery tools based on evidence, cost, and athlete response.", "children": [{"id": "574cd136-92d7-4291-98c6-a3f14fd2fcbe", "type": "concept", "title": "Sleep, nutrition, hydration, deloads, and active recovery"}, {"id": "8a4863cb-61db-4c2a-9bbc-bbd9b926e6d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Massage, compression, cold water, heat, and mobility work"}, {"id": "cf9e804f-d2c6-471a-8f35-ad15e826414b", "type": "concept", "title": "Placebo, preference, and individual response"}]}]}, {"id": "f174da96-574a-49d6-a051-71703cc112d1", "type": "topic", "title": "Program Design, Session Planning, and Exercise Progression", 